  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Core Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the core requirements for \"Cashback Link.\" My focus is on feature identification: the name, primary goal (URL conversion for Shopee, TikTok Shop, and Lazada), and platform detection/URL normalization (starting with Shopee). I\'m carefully outlining each function to ensure the correct conversion.\n\n\n**Expanding Platform Recognition**\n\nI\'ve expanded the platform recognition capabilities, particularly for Shopee. I can now handle multiple international domains like `shopee.co.id`, `shopee.vn`, etc. I am also working on robust ID extraction and cleaning for Shopee, ensuring the links are standardized. My next focus is on TikTok Shop\'s domain and URL parsing.\n\n\n**Refining Lazada URL Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the Lazada URL handling. I can extract clean product slugs, stripping extraneous parameters like `exlaz`, `spm`, and `click_id`. My goal is to standardize the output format. For mock affiliate link generation, I need to ensure a consistent format. I\'m focusing on the `s.lazada.co` format and the `www.lazada.com` format for products.\n\n\n**Adding User Configurable Features**\n\nI am now adding configurable user features. This involves allowing custom Affiliate Tags, Sub IDs, and Campaign Tags, showing instant URL transformations. I\'m calculating the estimated cashback rate and amount, and I\'m adding a toggle for SubID modes. I am preparing to implement one-click link copy and a safe external open button. I\'m also preparing for the implementation of a QR code generator.\n\n\n**Implementing User Interface**\n\nI am now focusing on the user interface, incorporating several key features. I\'m adding a history and saved links section, utilizing local storage for converted links with relevant information. I\'m also implementing a full dark mode toggle and a batch/multi-link converter mode for user convenience. I\'m preparing an affiliate calculator and rates guide and refining the visual styling. The goal is a sleek, modern, mobile-first design with Tailwind CSS.\n\n\n**Structuring Codebase Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a structured codebase with clearly defined components and types. I\'m building out a component hierarchy. I am organizing into a modular design. The focus will be on maintainability and easy feature expansion. The directories I\'ve defined are: `/src/types.ts`, `/src/lib/utils.ts`, `/src/components/Header.tsx`, `/src/components/UrlConverter.tsx`, `/src/components/ConversionResult.tsx`, `/src/components/QrCodeModal.tsx`, `/src/components/BatchConverter.tsx`, and `/src/components/HistoryList.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 622352563
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
